# {{PROJECT_NAME}} — Agent Instructions

Scope: this entire `{{PROJECT_SLUG}}` game repository.

This repo was stamped by the Ship Shit Games new-repo scaffolder
(`shipshitgames new`). It ships a single {{GENRE_TITLE}} game built on the
canonical org engine.

## Agent Entry Point

- Read `.agents/memory/MEMORY.md` first.
- Read `.agents/memory/repo-boundary.md` before moving apps, packages, or assets.
- Claude Code and Codex both follow this `AGENTS.md`; `.codex/instructions.md`
  points back here.
- Durable project memory lives in `.agents/memory/`. The `.claude/` and
  `.codex/` directories symlink their `memory/` and `skills/` into `.agents/`,
  so every agent shares one source of truth.

## Project Role

- This repo ships **{{PROJECT_NAME}}**, a {{GENRE_TITLE}} title.
- It consumes the canonical engine from `{{ENGINE_PACKAGE}}` — it does **not**
  fork or vendor a divergent engine. Engine changes belong upstream in
  `shipshitgames/shipshit.games`.
- Deadrot canon is vendored as the lore git submodule at `{{LORE_PATH}}`.
  Run `git submodule update --init {{LORE_PATH}}` after cloning.

## Engineering Rules

- Use Bun for package management unless a subproject explicitly requires npm.
- Keep gameplay loops imperative and Three.js-centered; keep React for UI
  overlays and shells only.
- Engine code must never encode game canon. Pass game content into
  `{{ENGINE_PACKAGE}}` seams as data or callbacks (see the `shipshit-engine`
  skill).
- Do not commit secrets, `.env` files, generated `dist`, `node_modules`, or
  local editor state.
- Inspect `git status` before edits and commit only the requested scope.

## GitHub Workflow

- When picking up an issue or board item, move it to `In Progress` before
  starting implementation.
- Use the `worktree` skill to branch off an issue (`feat/<number>-<slug>`).

## Skills

Curated skills live in `.agents/skills/`:

- `session-start` / `session-end` — load and persist context per session.
- `worktree` — branch off a GitHub issue/PR into an isolated worktree.
- `shipshit-engine` — how to consume `{{ENGINE_PACKAGE}}`.
- `vibe-game-workflow` — the build loop from idea to playable.
- `{{GENRE}}` — {{GENRE_TITLE}}-specific conventions for this game.
